{"route":"/docs/5.2/helpers/stretched-link/","version":"5.2","renderedVersion":"5.2","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Stretched link","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Make any HTML element or Bootstrap component clickable by “stretching” a nested link via CSS."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Add <code>.stretched-link</code> to a link to make its <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Containing_block\">containing block</a> clickable via a <code>::after</code> pseudo element. In most cases, this means that an element with <code>position: relative;</code> that contains a link with the <code>.stretched-link</code> class is clickable. Please note given <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/visuren.html#propdef-position\">how CSS <code>position</code> works</a>, <code>.stretched-link</code> cannot be mixed with most table elements."},{"id":"content--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Cards have <code>position: relative</code> by default in Bootstrap, so in this case you can safely add the <code>.stretched-link</code> class to a link in the card without any other HTML changes."},{"id":"content--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Multiple links and tap targets are not recommended with stretched links. However, some <code>position</code> and <code>z-index</code> styles can help should this be required."},{"id":"content--example-1","type":"demo","key":"9cf3bee37f438b076635","height":300},{"id":"content--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <img src=\"...\" class=\"card-img-top\" alt=\"...\">\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched link</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card's content.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"btn btn-primary stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"content--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Most custom components do not have <code>position: relative</code> by default, so we need to add the <code>.position-relative</code> here to prevent the link from stretching outside the parent element."},{"id":"content--example-2","type":"demo","key":"a99cba7693a736b632f3","height":147},{"id":"content--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"d-flex position-relative\">\n  <img src=\"...\" class=\"flex-shrink-0 me-3\" alt=\"...\">\n  <div>\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Custom component with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>This is some placeholder content for the custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we're using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"content--example-3","type":"demo","key":"be0d301543755b3b633d","height":147},{"id":"content--code-3","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"row g-0 bg-light position-relative\">\n  <div class=\"col-md-6 mb-md-0 p-md-4\">\n    <img src=\"...\" class=\"w-100\" alt=\"...\">\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"col-md-6 p-4 ps-md-0\">\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Columns with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>Another instance of placeholder content for this other custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we're using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block","type":"heading","en":"Identifying the containing block","level":2},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If the stretched link doesn’t seem to work, the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Containing_block#Identifying_the_containing_block\">containing block</a> will probably be the cause. The following CSS properties will make an element the containing block:"},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-1","type":"item","en":"A <code>position</code> value other than <code>static</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-2","type":"item","en":"A <code>transform</code> or <code>perspective</code> value other than <code>none</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-3","type":"item","en":"A <code>will-change</code> value of <code>transform</code> or <code>perspective</code>"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--item-4","type":"item","en":"A <code>filter</code> value other than <code>none</code> or a <code>will-change</code> value of <code>filter</code> (only works on Firefox)"}]}]},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--example-1","type":"demo","key":"578fdcac79e915a5f5b4","height":300},{"id":"identifying-the-containing-block--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <img src=\"...\" class=\"card-img-top\" alt=\"...\">\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched links</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card's content.</p>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">\n      <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link text-danger\" style=\"position: relative;\">Stretched link will not work here, because <code>position: relative</code> is added to the link</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"card-text bg-light\" style=\"transform: rotate(0);\">\n      This <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-warning stretched-link\">stretched link</a> will only be spread over the <code>p</code>-tag, because a transform is applied to it.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"}],"demos":[{"key":"9cf3bee37f438b076635","html":"\n<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <svg class=\"bd-placeholder-img card-img-top\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Card image cap\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" focusable=\"false\"><title>Card image cap</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#868e96\"></rect></svg>\n\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched link</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card's content.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"btn btn-primary stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"a99cba7693a736b632f3","html":"\n<div class=\"d-flex position-relative\">\n  <svg class=\"bd-placeholder-img flex-shrink-0 me-3\" width=\"144\" height=\"144\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Generic placeholder image\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" focusable=\"false\"><title>Generic placeholder image</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#868e96\"></rect></svg>\n\n  <div>\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Custom component with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>This is some placeholder content for the custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we're using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"be0d301543755b3b633d","html":"\n<div class=\"row g-0 bg-light position-relative\">\n  <div class=\"col-md-6 mb-md-0 p-md-4\">\n    <svg class=\"bd-placeholder-img w-100\" width=\"100%\" height=\"200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Generic placeholder image\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" focusable=\"false\"><title>Generic placeholder image</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#868e96\"></rect></svg>\n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"col-md-6 p-4 ps-md-0\">\n    <h5 class=\"mt-0\">Columns with stretched link</h5>\n    <p>Another instance of placeholder content for this other custom component. It is intended to mimic what some real-world content would look like, and we're using it here to give the component a bit of body and size.</p>\n    <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link\">Go somewhere</a>\n  </div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"578fdcac79e915a5f5b4","html":"\n<div class=\"card\" style=\"width: 18rem;\">\n  <svg class=\"bd-placeholder-img card-img-top\" width=\"100%\" height=\"180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Card image cap\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\" focusable=\"false\"><title>Card image cap</title><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#868e96\"></rect></svg>\n\n  <div class=\"card-body\">\n    <h5 class=\"card-title\">Card with stretched links</h5>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">Some quick example text to build on the card title and make up the bulk of the card's content.</p>\n    <p class=\"card-text\">\n      <a href=\"#\" class=\"stretched-link text-danger\" style=\"position: relative;\">Stretched link will not work here, because <code>position: relative</code> is added to the link</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"card-text bg-light\" style=\"transform: rotate(0);\">\n      This <a href=\"#\" class=\"text-warning stretched-link\">stretched link</a> will only be spread over the <code>p</code>-tag, because a transform is applied to it.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.2/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href"